## Cute Halloween Nail Colors (Beyond Black and Orange)

Black and orange are not the only Halloween colours, they are just the most obvious ones. <strong>Cute Halloween nails</strong> lean on an entirely different palette: blush pink, lavender, milky white, sage green, and the occasional pop of pastel purple, all of which carry the season without defaulting to the traditional scheme.

Blush pink softens absolutely anything painted on top of it, which is why it shows up under more ghost and pumpkin designs than any other single shade. Lavender does something slightly different, it reads as seasonal and slightly mystical without tipping into anything dark, which makes it a natural fit for anything with a "witchy but soft" angle. Milky white works almost like a blank canvas, a near-sheer base that lets whatever you paint on top, ghosts especially, stand out crisply against it.

Industry colour guidance backs this shift too. <a href='https://www.nailpro.com/nail-art/trends/article/21648128/halloween-nail-art-hues-and-tools-for-spooky-season'>industry nail experts</a> have pointed to purples and softer seasonal tones sitting alongside the traditional black and orange palette this year, which lines up with exactly the kind of pastel-forward set this section is describing. Sage green and dusty lilac round out the extended palette for anyone who wants their Halloween nails to double as a genuinely wearable everyday manicure through the rest of autumn.

